1
00:00:00,940 --> 00:00:05,340
A scripted scheduler for Taller Aurora, a fictional hiring co-op.

2
00:00:05,370 --> 00:00:10,810
A slot books only after the candidate confirms that exact slot. Offline. No
key.

3
00:00:12,040 --> 00:00:18,030
Candidate One asks for Ana Luz on April fourteenth twenty twenty-six, Buenos
Aires time.

4
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:22,570
Three options. Candidate confirms option one: nine o'clock.

5
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:31,660
Hold, then book on the internal calendar. The invite email stays
PENDING_APPROVAL. Nothing was sent yet.

6
00:00:32,930 --> 00:00:39,400
A simulated recruiter approves that same call. Outbox one, booked one,
terminal completed.

7
00:00:39,460 --> 00:00:44,600
An approval of ten o'clock would not cover eleven. The hash binds tool and
arguments.

8
00:00:45,750 --> 00:00:50,800
The expensive mistakes are a wrong slot and an invite that leaves before
anyone approves.

9
00:00:50,850 --> 00:00:59,590
Not covered: a real calendar, an authenticated recruiter channel, or live
model quality. Live mode on this revision is UNVERIFIED.

10
00:00:59,620 --> 00:01:05,420
Run python -m scheduling_agent demo. Lab path cost: zero.

